.TH geectl-pull-request-cleanup 1  "geectl-pull-request-cleanup 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-pull\-request\-cleanup \- Clean the local build roots for the submit request filed from the working copy in the current directory, when that request is accepted. The request id was recorded by `submit` in the checkout; the leaf reads the request state once and wipes the roots only on `accepted`. A request in any other state, and a checkout with nothing recorded, delete nothing. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl pull\-request cleanup\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clean the local build roots for the submit request filed from the working copy in the current directory, when that request is accepted. The request id was recorded by `submit` in the checkout; the leaf reads the request state once and wipes the roots only on `accepted`. A request in any other state, and a checkout with nothing recorded, delete nothing. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
